  "summary": "I own business-critical systems in Microsoft’s commercial channel — the source of truth for what customers are entitled to and using. Purchases, renewals, usage changes, Office, Azure, hardware, and third-party solutions all flow through systems my team designs and operates. Billions in enterprise revenue move through them every year.\n\nMy default is to design for scale, business continuity, and multi-tenancy from the start. I care about the parts that make software survive production: clear boundaries, progressive rollout, observability, runbooks, and the operational patterns on-call engineers need when something breaks at 3 AM.\n\nLately, I’ve been helping move our agentic AI work from experiments into production: agents, shared tooling, plugins, and memory-enabled workflows that help teams investigate incidents faster, reduce code review friction, improve observability, and apply AI safely in real engineering systems.",
